# 1. EXECUTIVE OBJECTIVE

## 1.1 Purpose

Kea Parrot has no prototype yet (confirmed 2026-11-20). The objective of this project is to build it from a greenfield foundation (Readiness R0) into a complete, dependable, secure, maintainable, performant and production-ready application.

This is not a request to introduce new features indiscriminately beyond the approved Master PRD (KEA-PRD-001).

The coding agent must build from the Readiness R0 foundation, following the approved Master PRD (KEA-PRD-001), and progressively bring every approved component to production standards. There is no existing implementation to investigate.

The transformation must cover:

- Functional completeness.
- Frontend and backend integration.
- Database integrity.
- Authentication and authorisation.
- Application security.
- Real-time functionality.
- User experience and interface consistency.
- Mobile and desktop responsiveness.
- Performance and scalability.
- Error handling and recovery.
- Testing and quality assurance.
- Monitoring and observability.
- Deployment and release management.
- Documentation and maintainability.
- Privacy and regulatory readiness.

## 1.2 Final objective

At completion, Kea Parrot must function as a real application, not a demonstration or experimental prototype.

It must function as a real application where:

1. Every production-approved feature performs its intended function.
2. Every interactive interface is connected to its correct backend operation.
3. Every important action is validated and securely processed.
4. Data persists correctly and remains consistent.
5. Real-time functionality works without requiring manual page refreshes.
6. Users can navigate the application reliably on mobile, tablet and desktop.
7. Errors are handled gracefully and do not silently corrupt application state.
8. Administrative and moderation capabilities operate securely.
9. Critical user journeys are tested and demonstrably functional.
10. The application can be deployed, monitored, maintained and recovered.

**Definition of success:** A user should be able to use Kea Parrot as a real product, not encounter a collection of partially functional screens.

