- Documentation.

Identify gaps between the foundation and the approved specifications, and any duplicated or disconnected planned components.

Do not remove foundation items merely because they appear unused. Establish whether they are referenced or required first.

## 3.2 Database investigation

Design and plan the database from KEA-DBS-002. The first migration creates the schema; there is no connected database or migration history to inspect yet.

Review:

- All planned tables.
- Columns and data types.
- Primary and foreign keys.
- Unique constraints.
- Indexes.
- Enums.
- Triggers.
- Functions.
- Views.
- RLS policies.
