# 14. PRODUCTION READINESS ACCEPTANCE GATES

The application must pass every mandatory gate before public production release.

| Gate | Requirement | Release condition |
|---|---|---|
| PR-01 | Repository audit | Complete |
| PR-02 | Feature completeness | All approved MVP features verified |
| PR-03 | Authentication | Critical flows pass |
| PR-04 | Authorisation | No unresolved critical access-control defects |
| PR-05 | Database integrity | No unresolved critical data-integrity defects |
| PR-06 | RLS and backend security | Required policies tested |
| PR-07 | Realtime | Critical approved flows verified |
| PR-08 | Mobile UX | Primary journeys pass |
| PR-09 | Accessibility | Agreed WCAG 2.2 AA checks completed |
| PR-10 | Performance | Agreed performance targets measured |
| PR-11 | Automated testing | Required suites pass |
| PR-12 | Monitoring | Operational monitoring active |
| PR-13 | Backups | Backup and recovery verified |
| PR-14 | Deployment | Staging and production procedures verified |
| PR-15 | Privacy | Required technical controls and legal review completed |
| PR-16 | Documentation | Operational documentation complete |

A gate cannot be marked complete without evidence.

## 14.1 Severity definitions

**P0 — Critical**

Immediate security, privacy, data-loss or system-integrity threat. Blocks release and may require immediate incident response.

**P1 — High**

Major feature failure, serious access-control weakness, broken primary journey or significant reliability problem. Blocks release.

**P2 — Medium**

Non-critical defect or degraded functionality with an acceptable documented workaround. Requires a planned fix and approval before release.

**P3 — Low**

Minor visual or operational issue with limited user impact. May be deferred with documented acceptance.

No P0 or P1 issue may remain unresolved at production release.

